  "applies_to": "Fox Thermal Instruments FT2 thermal mass gas flow meters on Modbus, read by a BASgatewayLX.",
  "summary": "Gateway profile for the Fox FT2: 31 objects (15 AI, 16 BI), all polled. Inputs give flow, total, temperature, elapsed time and velocity (raw and in the selected units, plus scaled copies) and status bits for power-up, limits, sensor range, calibration, settings, simulation, outputs, Anybus, RTC and CRC errors.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "Built from Contemporary Controls' BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile Fox_Thermal_Instuments_Model_FT2_LX.csv; the profile maps the registers in the maker's Modbus register document (https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/FoxThermalFT2.pdf).",
    "Object instances are the ones this profile assigns when it is loaded into the gateway. A site that edited or rebuilt the profile may use different instances.",
    "All 31 rows are flagged for polling in the profile, so every object is served to BACnet once the profile is loaded.",
    "The CSV has no read/write column: Analog/Binary Inputs are read-only and Analog/Binary Outputs are commandable (priority array), which is how the gateway maps them (access inferred). Descriptions give the Modbus register each object reads.",
    "Some names appear more than once in the profile as published (Status Flow rate reached high limit threshold); they are kept as printed and told apart by instance."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile Fox_Thermal_Instuments_Model_FT2",
    "doc_number": "Fox_Thermal_Instuments_Model_FT2_LX.csv",
